## Finding

`pkix-chain/src/lib.rs:188-190`:

```rust
fn _accepts(_v: &DefaultVerifier) {}
let _v: &pkix_path::DefaultVerifier = &DefaultVerifier;
_accepts(_v);
```

Two clippy issues:

1. `clippy::used_underscore_binding` — `_v` is bound with leading underscore (signaling "intentionally unused") and then immediately used.
2. `clippy::trivially_copy_pass_by_ref` — `&DefaultVerifier` is a 0-byte ZST passed by reference.

## Context

This is a `#[test]` that exists only to assert at compile time that `pkix_chain::DefaultVerifier == pkix_path::DefaultVerifier` (re-export type identity). The pattern is a deliberate smoke test, but the names are misleading.

## Fix

```rust
#[test]
fn default_verifier_reexport_type_identity() {
    fn accepts(_: &DefaultVerifier) {}
    let v: &pkix_path::DefaultVerifier = &DefaultVerifier;
    accepts(v);
}
```

Or inline as a const-eval check:

```rust
const _: fn(&DefaultVerifier) = |_: &pkix_path::DefaultVerifier| {};
```

## Priority

P4 — test-only clarity nit.
